186165421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165416 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165416 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165416 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c0a3ff9d-4c25-52f6-a5ce-1978a3171c0c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165417 #edb/ref 1080 "-sech x\\tanh x + 2csch x\\coth x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165417 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165417 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a37b7bde-4f5b-5f94-ac7b-2867bcc3fc5d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165418 #edb/ref 1080 "sech x(\\tanh x + 2csch x)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165418 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165418 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ad24ffb3-5e6c-5b09-9fe3-18f2e715f06e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165419 #edb/ref 1080 "-sech x\\tanh x + 2csch^{2} x\\coth x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165419 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165419 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2afe7502-3eab-5309-8390-1399d0c80e85" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165420 #edb/ref 1080 "sech x\\tanh x - 2csch^{2} x\\coth x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165420 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165420 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "389bb1c5-9ced-5f0a-b45a-cb801c45266a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165421 #edb/ref 1080 "sech x(-\\tanh x - 2sech x)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165421 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165421 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7fc9e493-b4b6-5f9f-a391-130f2cbea0fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166599 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8349" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166599 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $y = 3\\sech{x}+\\coth{x}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166599 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3817c58a-1176-5347-aa96-2846969cae32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166599 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nFirst, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic reciprocal hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n(\\sech x)' = -\\sech x\\tanh x, \\quad (\\csch x)' = -\\csch x \\coth x, \\quad (\\coth x)' = -\\csch^2 x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results and the rules of differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(3sech x + \\coth x) \\\\\n&= 3\\frac{d}{dx}(sech x) + \\frac{d}{dx}(\\coth x) \\\\\n&= 3(-sech x\\tanh x) + (-csch^{2} x) \\\\\n&=-3sech x\\tanh x - csch^{2} x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166600 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8350" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166600 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x) =\\coth(5x - 2)$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166600 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b14f0558-456d-51a9-85ac-0b36158bc52e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166600 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf =\\coth{g}, \\qquad g = 5x - 2\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}f} {\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}f} {\\textrm{d}g} \\cdot \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}g} {\\textrm{d}x}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}f} {\\textrm{d}g} = -\\csch^2{g}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}g} {\\textrm{d}x} = 5\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{df}{dx} &= -csch^{2} g \\cdot 5 \\\\\n&=-5csch^{2} g \\\\\n&=-5csch^{2} (5x - 2)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166601 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8351" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166601 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x) = x^2\\coth{x}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166601 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4baa8799-f8ce-521e-833b-8b66c747e701" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166601 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nHere, we have the product of two functions $u(x) = x^2$ and\n\n$$\nv(x) = \\coth{x}\n$$\n\nSo, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= (x^{2})^{′} \\cdot \\coth x + x^{2} \\cdot (\\coth x)^{′} \\\\\n&= 2x \\cdot \\coth x + x^{2} \\cdot (-csch^{2} x) \\\\\n&= x(2\\coth x - xcsch^{2} x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166602 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8352" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166602 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x) = \\dfrac{\\sech{x}}{4x}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166602 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bec9b472-31ce-5892-8a17-c4aa3c33ef12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166602 #edb/ref 1074 "$$\n\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{u(x)}{v(x)}\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\nu(x) = \\sech{x}\n$$\n\nand $v(x) = 4x$.\n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= (u^{′}(x) \\cdot v(x) - u(x) \\cdot v^{′}(x))/([v(x)]^{2}) \\\\\n&= ((sech x)^{′} \\cdot (4x) - sech x \\cdot (4x)^{′})/((4x)^{2}) \\\\\n&= ((-sech x\\tanh x) \\cdot (4x) - sech x \\cdot 4)/(16x^{2}) \\\\\n&= - (4sech x(x\\tanh x + 1))/(16x^{2}) \\\\\n&= - (sech x(x\\tanh x + 1))/(4x^{2})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166761 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166761 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167341 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166761 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167368 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166761 #edb/ref 1039 "Basic Derivatives of the Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166761 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186166599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166761 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "597e3939-e6b4-5237-a16e-8bae92f9b656" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166762 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166762 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167342 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166762 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166762 #edb/ref 1039 "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Chain Rule" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166762 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186166600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166762 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "6fd03e86-fa